+#!/bin/bash
+# The main display goes, and comes back, with NO ARBOR: the control of probe-the-main-display-goes.sh, whose header has the question, the rule written before the answer, the windows, the
+# rounds and how to read the output. What macOS and the apps do by themselves: the same windows at the same places, the same changes, the same lines.
+#
+#   scripts/mac-shell/run.sh --no-preflight "<why>" scripts/mac-shell/probe-the-main-display-goes.sh scripts/mac-shell/probe-the-main-display-goes-control.sh
+#
+# By itself or in one dispatch with the other, in either order: it builds the tools it needs (no Arbor) and leaves the Mac as it found it.
+# Why no pre-flight: the fake Mac has no stand-in for vdisplay, apptool or the sampler, so a rehearsal ends with exit code 2 before the first step.
+#
+# THE TIME, reckoned as in the other's header: the tools' build (36 s in an earlier control), the Mac, five windows and A's first coming (40 s); R1, 16 s; R3 five times, 130 to 165 s; R2,
+# 16 s; the end, 15 s. FOUR AND A QUARTER TO FIVE MINUTES. No round begins after 500 s (JOURNEY_BUDGET); lib.sh ends the script at 1,020 s.
+#
+# WHAT DIFFERS. R1 once, R3 FIVE times, R2 once. The steps are m-<round>-…. There is no trace: `told` is `no Arbor` in every `word` line, there is no `word-trace`, and macOS's own
+# first word about its screens is in screens.log alone (N, R): if screens.swift does not compile, which the script says with a `!!!`, this script has no notice at all, `notice` is
+# `unknown`, and the list is new when a loop around `vdisplay list` sees it, some twenty times a second.
+# That no Arbor runs: `pgrep -x Arbor` at the step `arbor` (the script ends there if one does), before the part, after it, and after the last step; the script builds and starts none.
+#
+# Only on GitHub's Macs: it plugs a display in and out, changes which display is the main one, switches the display's size, changes Reduce Motion and puts it back, hides apps, opens
+# and quits four apps.
+JOURNEY_ARBOR=no
+JOURNEY_PARTS=G
+JOURNEY_REST=${JOURNEY_REST:-2}
+JOURNEY_BUDGET=${JOURNEY_BUDGET:-500}
+# As finely as the sampler goes.
+DAY_HZ=${DAY_HZ:-240}
+source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/probe-went-and-came-back-journey.sh"
